    "label": {
      "en": "Universal child benefit coefficient"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$bchnm_coef"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Coefficient (1.75) that multiplies the Basic Social Amount (BSA) to derive the monthly amount of the universal child benefit (išmoka vaikui) paid per dependent child. It is used in bchnm_lt/BenCalc (Comp_perElig, comment 'universal child benefit') to compute the per-child payment. Per the benefits documentation, this is a non-contributory monthly cash benefit of 1.75 BSA paid for each dependent child up to age 18 (or 23 if in full-time education), with no income test, indexed annually via the BSA uprating rule."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: constants for child benefits"
    },
